# ==========================================================================
#  ALLOWLIST, not a denylist.
#
#  Everything is ignored by default; only the tooling is added back. A
#  denylist fails open - one unmatched pattern and 75 MB of paid course
#  captures are in a commit and in the history forever. This direction fails
#  closed: a new file is invisible until someone deliberately un-ignores it.
#
#  If you add a file and git does not see it, that is this file working.
#  Check with:  git check-ignore -v <path>
# ==========================================================================

*

# --- the tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!START_HERE.md
!setup.sh
!setup.ps1
!PROFILE.md
!LICENSE
!scripts/
!scripts/*.py
!scripts/*.js
!scripts/*.md
!scripts/VERSION.json
!scripts/project_state.json

# --- folder skeleton, so a clone has the right shape ---------------------
!Source Files/
!Anki Decks/
!COMPLETED/
!work/
!*/.gitkeep
!Source Files/README.md
!Anki Decks/README.md
!COMPLETED/README.md

# --- the redacted worked example (invented content, safe to publish) -----
!COMPLETED/EXAMPLE/
!COMPLETED/EXAMPLE/**

# --- never, under any circumstances --------------------------------------
#  Belt and braces. The bare `*` above already covers these; they are spelled
#  out so the intent survives someone loosening a rule later.
*.pdf
*.apkg
*.docx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gdoc
work/**
scripts/_out/
scripts/work/
scripts/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# The one exception to the blanket *.json ignore is handled above by naming
# project_state.json and VERSION.json explicitly. Audit JSON from a real run
# stays out - it quotes card text.
